# Deno Deploy Platform Specification

> Boundary: this is an unpinned research snapshot for artifact work, not the
> Edge Canon application contract, a complete current vendor specification, or
> conformance/support evidence. Recheck claims against versioned official
> sources; current target status is generated from the locked registry.

This document records research used to build Deno-target artifacts.

## Platform Overview

**Deno Deploy** is a globally distributed JavaScript/TypeScript runtime built on V8.

- **Runtime**: Deno 2.x (V8 engine)
- **Languages**: JavaScript, TypeScript (native), WebAssembly
- **Network**: 35+ regions globally
- **Performance**: Near-instant cold starts

## Entry Point Format

### Standard Handler (Deno.serve)

```typescript
Deno.serve(async (req: Request): Promise<Response> => {
  return new Response("Hello World!");
});
```

### With Port Configuration

```typescript
Deno.serve({ port: 8000 }, async (req) => {
  return new Response("Hello on port 8000");
});
```

### With Handler Options

```typescript
Deno.serve({
  port: 8000,
  hostname: "0.0.0.0",
  onListen: ({ port, hostname }) => {
    console.log(`Server running on http://${hostname}:${port}`);
  }
}, handler);
```

## Handler Parameters

### Request Object

Standard Fetch API Request:

```typescript
interface Request {
  url: string;           // Full URL
  method: string;        // GET, POST, PUT, DELETE, etc.
  headers: Headers;      // Request headers
  body: ReadableStream | null;  // Request body

  // Request methods
  text(): Promise<string>;
  json(): Promise<any>;
  formData(): Promise<FormData>;
  arrayBuffer(): Promise<ArrayBuffer>;
  blob(): Promise<Blob>;
}
```

**URL parsing:**
```typescript
const url = new URL(req.url);
const pathname = url.pathname;
const searchParams = url.searchParams;
```

### Response Object

Standard Fetch API Response:

```typescript
// Text response
new Response("Hello World", {
  status: 200,
  headers: { "content-type": "text/plain" }
});

// JSON response
new Response(JSON.stringify({ message: "Hello" }), {
  headers: { "content-type": "application/json" }
});

// Redirect
Response.redirect("https://example.com", 302);

// Stream response
new Response(readableStream, {
  headers: {
    "content-type": "text/event-stream",
    "cache-control": "no-cache"
  }
});
```

