## Deno APIs Available

### File System (Read-only for deployed code)

```typescript
// Read file
const text = await Deno.readTextFile("./data.txt");

// Read directory
for await (const entry of Deno.readDir("./")) {
  console.log(entry.name);
}

// Get file info
const fileInfo = await Deno.stat("./file.txt");
```

**⚠️ Write operations only work locally, not in deployed code**

### Network APIs

```typescript
// HTTP fetch
const response = await fetch("https://api.example.com/data");

// TCP connection
const conn = await Deno.connect({ hostname: "example.com", port: 80 });

// TLS connection
const tlsConn = await Deno.connectTls({ hostname: "example.com", port: 443 });

// DNS lookup
const records = await Deno.resolveDns("example.com", "A");
```

### Crypto API

```typescript
// Generate random values
const bytes = crypto.getRandomValues(new Uint8Array(16));

// Generate UUID
const uuid = crypto.randomUUID();

// Hashing
const data = new TextEncoder().encode("Hello");
const hashBuffer = await crypto.subtle.digest("SHA-256", data);
```

### Web Platform APIs

All standard Web APIs:
- `fetch()`, `Request`, `Response`, `Headers`
- `URL`, `URLSearchParams`, `URLPattern`
- `TextEncoder`, `TextDecoder`
- `ReadableStream`, `WritableStream`, `TransformStream`
- `setTimeout()`, `setInterval()`, `clearTimeout()`, `clearInterval`
- `console.*`
- `atob()`, `btoa()`
- `structuredClone()`
