## Deno KV (Key-Value Database)

### Opening Database

```typescript
const kv = await Deno.openKv();
```

### Basic Operations

```typescript
// Set value
await kv.set(["users", "alice"], { name: "Alice", age: 30 });

// Get value
const entry = await kv.get(["users", "alice"]);
console.log(entry.value); // { name: "Alice", age: 30 }

// Delete
await kv.delete(["users", "alice"]);

// Atomic operations
const result = await kv.atomic()
  .check({ key: ["counter"], versionstamp: null })
  .set(["counter"], 1)
  .commit();
```

### Listing Keys

```typescript
// List all entries with prefix
const iter = kv.list({ prefix: ["users"] });
for await (const entry of iter) {
  console.log(entry.key, entry.value);
}

// List with pagination
const entries = kv.list({ prefix: ["users"] }, { limit: 10 });
```

### Watch for Changes

```typescript
const stream = kv.watch([["users", "alice"]]);
for await (const entries of stream) {
  console.log("Value changed:", entries[0].value);
}
```

## Database Integration

### Postgres

```typescript
import { Client } from "https://deno.land/x/postgres/mod.ts";

const client = new Client({
  user: Deno.env.get("DB_USER"),
  database: Deno.env.get("DB_NAME"),
  hostname: Deno.env.get("DB_HOST"),
  port: 5432,
  password: Deno.env.get("DB_PASSWORD"),
});

await client.connect();

const result = await client.queryObject`
  SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ${userId}
`;

await client.end();
```

### MongoDB

```typescript
import { MongoClient } from "https://deno.land/x/mongo/mod.ts";

const client = new MongoClient();
await client.connect(Deno.env.get("MONGO_URL"));

const db = client.database("mydb");
const users = db.collection("users");

const user = await users.findOne({ _id: userId });
```

