## Scheduled Tasks (Cron)

```typescript
// Define at module top level
Deno.cron("cleanup", "0 0 * * *", async () => {
  console.log("Running daily cleanup");
  // Cleanup logic
});

Deno.cron("hourly-sync", "0 * * * *", async () => {
  console.log("Hourly sync");
});

// Must also have a serve handler
Deno.serve(() => new Response("OK"));
```

**Cron syntax:** `minute hour day month weekday`

## BroadcastChannel (Cross-Instance Communication)

```typescript
const channel = new BroadcastChannel("my-channel");

// Send message
channel.postMessage({ type: "update", data: "value" });

// Receive messages
channel.onmessage = (event) => {
  console.log("Received:", event.data);
};
```

**Use case:** Synchronize state across multiple deployment instances

## Static Files

### Serving Static Assets

```typescript
Deno.serve(async (req) => {
  const url = new URL(req.url);

  // Serve static file
  if (url.pathname.startsWith("/static/")) {
    const filePath = `.${url.pathname}`;
    try {
      const file = await Deno.readFile(filePath);
      return new Response(file, {
        headers: { "content-type": "application/octet-stream" }
      });
    } catch {
      return new Response("Not Found", { status: 404 });
    }
  }

  return new Response("API");
});
```

### MIME Types

```typescript
import { contentType } from "https://deno.land/std/media_types/mod.ts";

const mimeType = contentType(".html"); // "text/html; charset=UTF-8"
```

## Limitations

### Deployment Constraints

| Constraint | Limit |
|------------|-------|
| Max deployment size | 20 MB |
| Max file count | 1000 files |
| Build timeout | 5-15 minutes (configurable) |
| Max environment variables | 100 |

### Runtime Constraints

| Constraint | Limit |
|------------|-------|
| Max request body | 100 MB |
| Max response body | Unlimited (streaming) |
| CPU time per request | No hard limit |
| Memory per isolate | ~512 MB soft limit |

### Forbidden Operations

❌ **Not allowed:**
- `Deno.run()` / `child_process`
- `worker_threads`
- Dynamic imports with non-static specifiers (external modules)
- File system writes in deployed code
- Forward proxies, VPNs
- Cryptocurrency mining
- Media hosting for external sites

✅ **Allowed:**
- All Web APIs
- File system reads (static assets)
- Database connections
- External API calls
- WebSockets

