## Deployment

### Via deployctl CLI

```bash
# Install deployctl
deno install -Arf jsr:@deno/deployctl

# Deploy
deployctl deploy --project=my-project main.ts

# Deploy with environment variables
deployctl deploy \
  --project=my-project \
  --env=API_KEY=secret \
  main.ts

# Production deployment
deployctl deploy --prod main.ts
```

### Via GitHub Integration

1. Connect GitHub repository in Dashboard
2. Push to main branch
3. Automatic deployment triggered

**Deployment config (.github/workflows/deploy.yml):**
```yaml
name: Deploy
on:
  push:
    branches: [main]

jobs:
  deploy:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v3
      - uses: denoland/deployctl@v1
        with:
          project: my-project
          entrypoint: main.ts
          root: .
```

### Via Dashboard

Upload via web interface at dash.deno.com/projects

## Routing

### Manual Routing

```typescript
Deno.serve(async (req) => {
  const url = new URL(req.url);

  if (url.pathname === "/") {
    return new Response("Home");
  }

  if (url.pathname === "/api/users") {
    return new Response(JSON.stringify(users));
  }

  return new Response("Not Found", { status: 404 });
});
```

### Using URLPattern

```typescript
const patterns = {
  home: new URLPattern({ pathname: "/" }),
  user: new URLPattern({ pathname: "/users/:id" }),
};

Deno.serve((req) => {
  const url = new URL(req.url);

  if (patterns.home.test(url)) {
    return new Response("Home");
  }

  const userMatch = patterns.user.exec(url);
  if (userMatch) {
    const userId = userMatch.pathname.groups.id;
    return new Response(`User: ${userId}`);
  }

  return new Response("Not Found", { status: 404 });
});
```

### Using Framework (Fresh, Hono)

**Fresh (Deno-first framework):**
```typescript
// routes/index.tsx
export default function Home() {
  return <h1>Welcome to Fresh!</h1>;
}
```

**Hono (Lightweight router):**
```typescript
import { Hono } from "https://deno.land/x/hono/mod.ts";

const app = new Hono();

app.get("/", (c) => c.text("Hello!"));
app.get("/users/:id", (c) => {
  return c.json({ id: c.req.param("id") });
});

Deno.serve(app.fetch);
```

## Error Handling

```typescript
Deno.serve(async (req) => {
  try {
    const url = new URL(req.url);

    // Your logic
    if (url.pathname === "/error") {
      throw new Error("Something went wrong");
    }

    return new Response("OK");
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("Error:", error);

    return new Response(
      JSON.stringify({ error: error.message }),
      {
        status: 500,
        headers: { "content-type": "application/json" }
      }
    );
  }
});
```

